      "id": "S45B-PRIMARY-BLOCKER-001",
      "severity": "BLOCKER",
      "title": "Pre-output formal failures consume the permanent lock without a retained failure receipt",
      "file": "/Users/rocket/Desktop/HKUST IT/ip-/geometry-world-modeling/work/S45B_c1_numeric_camera_guard_preparation/camera_guard.py",
      "lines": [
        1145,
        1198,
        1281,
        1333
      ],
      "finding": "main create-exclusively acquires .c1_numeric_camera_guard.lock and then calls formal_run. Before execution_01 exists, before the receipt object is constructed, and outside the numeric try/except, formal_run validates the fixed output argument, static identities, both source reviews, the binding and binding review, all upstream metadata, and the archive event chain. Any error or interruption in that interval propagates through main's finally, which only closes descriptors. The empty lock remains forever, execution_01 and receipt.json remain absent, and a correct retry is prohibited.",
      "independent_static_evidence": {
        "lock_created_before_formal_run": true,
        "pre_output_checks": [
          "fixed out value",
          "verify_static_reference",
          "verify_source_reviews",
          "verify_binding",
          "verify_upstream",
          "selected_event_captures"
        ],
        "receipt_created_after_output_mkdir": true,
        "outer_formal_run_exception_handler": false,
        "lock_removed": false,
        "structured_failure_artifact_written": false
      },
      "protocol_conflict": "PROTOCOL section 5 promises that every failure is retained and that the single attempt is auditable. An unexplained empty lock proves only that a pathname was consumed; it does not retain start time, supplied identity hashes, failed phase, exception, completion time, or the zero-body boundary.",
      "required_fix": "Retain an immutable structured receipt for every failure after the permanent lock is acquired, including all pre-output/pre-tensor phases. The record must be written through a stable create-only path or into the held lock inode, include the failed phase and zero/body counters, and preserve the no-retry rule. Update protocol and synthetic negative tests, then rehash all four files and obtain two new source reviews."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45B-PRIMARY-BLOCKER-002",
      "severity": "BLOCKER",
      "title": "The lock pathname is not revalidated after the initial inode check",
      "file": "/Users/rocket/Desktop/HKUST IT/ip-/geometry-world-modeling/work/S45B_c1_numeric_camera_guard_preparation/camera_guard.py",
      "lines": [
        1316,
        1332
      ],
      "finding": "The lock FD and pathname are compared once before flock, but no later fstat-versus-path or st_nlink check occurs. If the pathname is unlinked and recreated while the first FD is held, flock remains attached to the unlinked old inode and another formal invocation can acquire a different inode at the same fixed path. The output directory lease is repeatedly revalidated; the claimed single-use lock lease is not.",
      "independent_static_evidence": {
        "lock_path_stat_calls_after_initial_check": 0,
        "lock_fd_fstat_calls_after_initial_check": 0,
        "lock_link_count_close_check": false,
        "lock_fd_held_until_formal_run_returns": true,
        "output_path_inode_revalidation_present": true
      },
      "required_fix": "Carry the lock FD and its initial identity into the formal path and revalidate fstat, pathname inode, regular-file type, and st_nlink before output creation, before each terminal write, and at close. Treat any mismatch as a retained terminal failure."
    }
